---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The lab"
  description="The Halden Distribution Ltd story, the lab architecture, the tools, and the honesty statement behind this portfolio."
>
  <h1>The lab</h1>

  <section>
    <h2>One simulated company for all ten projects</h2>
    <div class="problem-statement">
      <strong>Halden Distribution Ltd.</strong> (fictional): 85 staff, one head office, one
      warehouse, 12 remote sales staff. Departments: Management, Finance, HR, Sales,
      Operations/Warehouse, and IT (me). The situation I inherited: a flat network, shared admin
      passwords, no MFA, ad-hoc backups nobody has tested, assets tracked in a spreadsheet, tickets
      arriving by email and WhatsApp, and 30% of PCs on Windows 10.
    </div>
    <p>
      Every project starts from that inherited state, fixes it, and measures the before/after. The
      domain is <code>ad.halden.internal</code> — <code>.internal</code> is the top-level domain
      ICANN reserved for private use in 2024.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Architecture</h2>
    <p class="small muted">
      The whole environment runs as virtual machines on one physical host, and it is never exposed
      to the internet. After project P6 the network is split into firewall-enforced zones:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>VLAN</th><th>Zone</th><th>Subnet</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>10</td><td>SERVERS</td><td>192.168.10.0/24</td><td>Domain controllers, file server, app servers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>20</td><td>WAREHOUSE</td><td>192.168.20.0/24</td><td>Warehouse site behind its own firewall</td></tr>
        <tr><td>30</td><td>USERS-HQ</td><td>192.168.30.0/24</td><td>Staff workstations</td></tr>
        <tr><td>40</td><td>MGMT</td><td>192.168.40.0/24</td><td>Admin workstation (PAW), hypervisor, backup plane</td></tr>
        <tr><td>50</td><td>GUEST</td><td>192.168.50.0/24</td><td>Guest Wi-Fi, internet only</td></tr>
        <tr><td>60</td><td>IOT</td><td>192.168.60.0/24</td><td>Printers, CCTV, scanners</td></tr>
        <tr><td>—</td><td>VPN-USERS</td><td>192.168.70.0/24</td><td>Remote staff (MFA VPN)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tools in the lab</h2>
    <p>
      Windows Server 2025 and Windows 11 Enterprise (evaluation), Ubuntu Server 24.04, OPNsense,
      Active Directory, Entra ID (trial tenant), PowerShell, Python, Ansible, WSUS, Greenbone
      Community Edition, Wazuh, Sysmon, GLPI, BookStack, Uptime Kuma, restic, MinIO with Object
      Lock, Proxmox Backup Server or Veeam CE, PingCastle, BloodHound CE, HardeningKitty,
      Atomic Red Team, Power BI Desktop and draw.io. Everything used is free or an evaluation
      licence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Honesty statement</h2>
    <p>
      This is a <strong>home lab</strong>: a simulated company, on my own isolated hardware. The
      configurations are real, the measurements are real, and synthetic data (such as the 85-user HR
      file or the synthetic device fleet) is labelled as synthetic wherever it appears. The lab is
      listed on my CV under <em>Projects / Home Lab</em> — never as employment experience — and
      nothing here was run against any network I do not own.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
